<p style="text-align: center;"><img src="/images/2016/Vampy.jpg" alt="A painting of the fishing boat Vampy (WIP)" width="450" height="600" data-filename="29174728653_6fdb6e0e2c_o.jpg" /></p>
<p style="text-align: center;">Vampy (WIP). 12x12, oil on linen panel. 2016</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">You know it's been a long and difficult painting day when the trash bag that contains your discarded paper towels weighs more than the plywood panel you were painting on.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">This side view is a painting that I was working on and really struggling with today. I have already painted this in a smaller size (8x8), but it had a very different look, and when I tried scaling it up to the larger panel it didn't look so good. I decided to scrape off the morning's efforts and start from scratch this afternoon.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">I shifted to a viridian, alizarin, yellow ochre palette which is very oily and consequently the paint has a lot of shine. That's why I photographed it from the side for now. Updates to come when I have something more finished.</p>